; BUG-009 reproducer: bareword map member keys (e.g. `tld:`) are
; treated as unresolved type names during `.within` comparison.
; A bareword member key is a concrete text label, not a type
; reference.  `tld:` must compare successfully against `label =
; int / tstr` because `tld` is a single concrete text key that
; lies within `tstr`.

label = int / tstr
values = any
header-map = { * label => values }

specific = { tld: tstr, root: bstr } .within header-map